            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac tamponade as an unusual manifestation of infective endocarditis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>165-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2009.00960.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Contained rupture of the left ventricle secondary to a myocardial abscess is uncommon. We present a case of infective endocarditis of the aortic valve with an unusual manifestation: a cardiac tamponade due to a pseudoaneurysm of the left ventricle.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
